    "biography": {
      "concept": "Waiting on the Stillwater station platform for the 4:10 (Act 2)",
      "notes": "May Farrow sits on the platform bench at Stillwater station with her coat buttoned and her hands in her lap, entirely content. She is seeing her son Denny off on the 4:10 to his first job up the line, as soon as he's back from Bucky's lemonade stand. She checks her watch against the station clock, and the clock agrees with her. She is warm and unhurried and talks about Denny like someone expecting him to walk up at any second. She has opinions about Bucky's prices."
    }
